<title>USA: United Tech says aerospace unit led Q2 gain.</title>
<headline>United Tech says aerospace unit led Q2 gain.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Technologies Corp said Wednesday its aerospace unit Pratt &amp; Whitney led its 19 percent earnings gain to $1.17 a share in the second quarter, despite a strong dollar cutting into the company's profits by $0.04 a share.</p>
<p>The aerospace division posted an operating profit of $210 million on revenues of $1.94 billion in the quarter, compared with a $160 million profit on $1.53 billion in revenues the year before.</p>
